## Quick Setup

1. Copy this file to `.env.local`:
   ```bash
   cp ENV_TEMPLATE.md .env.local
   ```

2. Edit `.env.local` and replace all placeholder values

3. Never commit `.env.local` to version control!

## Getting Your Credentials

### Supabase
1. Create project at [supabase.com](https://supabase.com)
2. Go to Settings → API
3. Copy URL and keys
4. See [SUPABASE_SETUP.md](SUPABASE_SETUP.md) for details

### Airtable
1. Create base at [airtable.com](https://airtable.com)
2. Create Personal Access Token at [airtable.com/create/tokens](https://airtable.com/create/tokens)
3. Get Base ID from API documentation
4. See [AIRTABLE_SETUP.md](AIRTABLE_SETUP.md) for details

### JWT Secret
Generate a secure random secret:
```bash
openssl rand -base64 32
```

Or use Node.js:
```bash
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
```

## Production Configuration

For Vercel deployment:
1. Go to Vercel dashboard → Project Settings → Environment Variables
2. Add each variable individually
3. Set scope: Production, Preview, Development (as needed)
4. Never use the same JWT_SIGNING_SECRET for dev and production!

